# Does the batch's permutation symmetry, built into the GP KERNEL, buy anything?
#
# The enzyme design is a SET of m experiments and the loss is invariant to their order, so all m!
# orderings are one design. `permutation-invariant-rbf` averages the kernel over that group (one
# lengthscale per exchangeable block instead of one per slot); `ard-rbf` models no symmetry at all.
# Nothing else differs between the arms, so the difference in their curves IS the symmetry's worth.
#
# The random arm never touches the kernel, so ONE null serves both -- the analysis checks that the
# problem settings match before it lends the null out.
ard  |bo    |--kernel ard-rbf
pi   |bo    |--kernel permutation-invariant-rbf
null |random|
